float WaterShallowAlpha // the opacity of shallow river/lake water: a float from 0 to 1 on every row (proven from the bytes); which of the four floats is which is the public definitions' order, consistent with the bytes (shallow <= deep on 95 % of Retail rows; the same values in Retail and Classic on the rows they share) and with the Durotar reference fit (0.40 / 0.80), not proven
float WaterDeepAlpha // the opacity of deep river/lake water: as WaterShallowAlpha (Classic Era: by MoP Classic's layout and by elimination, inferred)
float OceanShallowAlpha // the opacity of shallow ocean: as WaterShallowAlpha (no ocean reference measured yet)
float OceanDeepAlpha // the opacity of deep ocean: as WaterShallowAlpha
int Flags // flags (Retail: 0x100 on 86 rows, 76 of them with OverrideSunPosition set (115 set overall); 0x200 on 41 rows, all with SunPolar and SunAzimuth set (69 set overall): proven from the bytes); the name is the public definitions', the meaning of each bit not established
