COMMENT Written for WoW Model Viewer's light catalogue (wow::LightCatalog: the zone light's water colours,
COMMENT docs/world-viewer/09-liquids.md, and the outdoor light, docs/world-viewer/10-light-sky-fog.md). The layouts come
COMMENT from public table definitions, read as hypotheses: the columns the catalogue reads (database.xml, table LightParams)
COMMENT were checked against the clients' own bytes (the four alphas in Stage 09; the shapes of the columns named in Stage
COMMENT 10); the other columns are named by their field index, their types and widths the hypotheses' (never read). A
COMMENT neutral name that two layouts share is the same slot in the column order (after Classic's inline ID), not an
COMMENT established equal meaning. Fields 0-29 are the same columns in CAE394E7 and A7F31923 (on all 3745 rows Retail and
COMMENT PTR share); A7F31923 inserts six fields at 30-35 (Added_30 to Added_35), so Retail's fields 30 and 31 are its 36
COMMENT and 37 -- equal on all 3745 shared rows, the next best column on 3739 and 136 (an earlier version of this file
COMMENT said fields 0-31 were the same: they are not). Every field is listed in file order. Most Retail rows are copy
COMMENT rows: LightData and Light refer to copy IDs directly. A layout not listed here is not read.

